{"id": "EUVD-2026-93191", "enisaUuid": "00de6a9b-c410-3873-aab8-024be4b71074", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nASoC: codecs: rt712-sdca-dmic: fix uninitialized stream_config->type\n\nstream_config is not initialized before being passed to\nsdw_stream_add_slave().  The type field may contain garbage and is\nlater copied to stream->type by sdw_config_stream().\n\nZero-initialize stream_config so type defaults to SDW_STREAM_PCM.\n\nWhile at it, use snd_sdw_params_to_config() helper instead of\nopen-coding the same logic.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:45:26", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:16:34", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6507055733a9d397289277408b52daf422f8a814", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c144447c207e2be24d6ac86d544691ba464caad8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d93988c9e58d37b677f6ee8aceae741c8d1e30ad", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a318ee718e7448cd6bf62d9b3197b6a6a8d4701e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/03a5699a0a04309c597683967aaaf25d1e555ea2"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98263", "GHSA-8pw2-wmm5-rgrf"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2652be29-6bb4-36db-84b8-5799f4c89742", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "63a511284c9ea72696a5dd0a2d2721bdef19f774 <d93988c9e58d37b677f6ee8aceae741c8d1e30ad"}, {"id": "3c4202b3-467e-38bf-8e5f-959787b00aae", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.4"}, {"id": "73c38486-6a95-39a9-842b-a61bcaf2a3c5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.54"}, {"id": "7934a0ae-a8bc-3f2b-9cbe-9491ca178b0d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "806598b1-c248-3412-b49f-b92a49e37b03", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "63a511284c9ea72696a5dd0a2d2721bdef19f774 <03a5699a0a04309c5